# Pure unadopted policy transfer descriptors and codec
Based on frozen3956329; only three new files. Existing readers, ledger, backup payload/checkpoint and Finance files unchanged. Closed four-policy registry imports immutable Metadata/SPECS; fixed field names, type/shape/percell/hexSHA validation. SQL builders return descriptions and bound parameters ONLY, never query. Conditional BYTEA transfer includes exact identity/type/bytecount/hash/cap predicates. This is not native SQL execution evidence or authorization/admission.
Codec accepts exactbytes or memoryview (nbytes checked before copy), checks exact bytecount+SHA before UTF8/JSON parse and returns fresh decoded containers each call, no cache. Generic errors suppress payload details. NaN/Infinity constants and overflowing Pythonfloat values such as1e999 hold. PostgreSQL numeric may represent such values finitely: this narrower finite-Python-number decoder is defensive engineering admission, NOT proof nativepolicyinvalid or fullnativeequivalence. No Decimal substitution/downstream type changes. Byte cap is NOT a JSON parse-depth/CPU limit.
Eight pure definitions pass normal/-O; recursion/overflow handler test uses explicit pure exception injection, not a measured decoder depth boundary. Original initial2000-level recursion assumption did not raise on this Python and was corrected to truthful handler-only testing.13existing ledger +5policy pure regressions also run; no orchestration/domain/ticket integration or ledger mutations. SQL/hash/UTF8 canonicality/ownwrite-transfer behavior and nativeSQL permissions remain UNRUN. No current PolicyCellBudget fingerprint/cache fix or consumer adoption yet. No routes/registry/migration/DB/provider/held operation.
